.TH NETSTAT 1 "2026" "KERNEL32" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
netstat \- etat du reseau / network status
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B netstat
[-antulpr]
.br
.B ss
[-antulp]
.br
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads /proc/net/tcp, /proc/net/udp, /proc/net/route and /proc/net/dev. -a all sockets, -l listening only, -t TCP, -u UDP, -r routing table, -i interfaces. ss
prints the same tables in its own layout.
.SH SEE ALSO
ifconfig(1), route(1)
